[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'In today\'s video, we\'re going to be checking out the new EG4 solar powered window air conditioner. Now, this thing can be powered 100% off of solar panels connected directly to it. It already has a built-in charge controller and'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'inverter. You can also power it by just plugging it into a standard electrical outlet, or you can do a combination of both. Anyone can install this thing in less than an hour, and that includes reading the instructions. So, it is very'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'DIY friendly. You can control this thing in a few different ways. One, obviously you\'ve got buttons on the front of the screen. You can control it there. Two, you can use the included remote. And three, there is a smartphone app for'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this thing where you can control it from anywhere in the world you have an internet connection. Obviously, as long as this is connected to your home Wi-Fi. Now, let\'s go into the specs on this thing. This is a 12K BTU unit, which means it can cool up to 600 square ft.'

[00:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Now, I\'m in a tiny home here that is 399 ft, but it\'s got 20 foot ceilings, so it\'s really tall. So, we\'ll see how it performs in this thing. Now, this unit does require your window to be from 24.9'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in to 39 in wide. The unit is 15 in tall, so your window will need to be, I don\'t know, an inch or two taller than that as well. Now, it has a CER rating of 14.2, which qualifies this with an'

[01:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Energy Star rating. So, it is very energy efficient if you do need to plug it in to the outlet 100% of the time. EG4 does recommend connecting at least 1,400 watts of solar panels to this unit with an operating voltage range of 75 to'

[01:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '350 volts. And to get this thing to basically turn on, you\'ll have to have a minimum of 100 volts coming from those solar panels. Now, from those solar panels, it\'s also rated to operate between 3.3 and 13 amps, but you'

[01:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'absolutely never want to go over 15. Now, the unit weighs a total of 66 lbs. I was able to lift it easily into this window. Now, if you do have two people, it will make it very easy to put in'

[01:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'place. It also comes with a 5-year warranty, which is a very good warranty for a 12K BTU window air conditioner. Now, I ended up going with a package where it includes solar panels with it. So, you don\'t have to do any of the'

[02:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'calculations, try to figure out volts or amps to fit this thing, right? So, if you want to just pick up that package, I will have a link to that in the description of this video or pinned in the comments below. Now, that comes with the unit, the seven solar panels, and'

[02:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
