AUDIO: 'thing is really doing well. So, the way we\'re going to use this is just get it as cold as it possibly can be in here and then once the sun goes down, just let the house slowly warm up. So, if I'

[06:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'have to put a sweater on in here, I don\'t mind that when it\'s 95° outside. Not to mention, if the grid power does go down with these super hot days in Texas, maybe the grid gets overloaded and they have to do some rolling'

[06:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'blackouts. Well, guess what? We\'ve got air conditioning in here. So, another important thing we need to discuss, I think, is uh the plug for this. It says in the manual that it says to put this on a 20 amp circuit. Now, this is a tiny house. This doesn\'t have 20 amp'

[06:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'circuits. And actually, NEC code allows for living room outlets to be 15 amps. Um, so can you still use this with on a 15 amp circuit? Well, we do and we have'

[06:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'no problems. Actually, I\'ve had another 12k BTU window air conditioner as well in this house that was just plugged into the 15 amp circuit and it did totally fine. Now, keep in mind that what I\'ve seen and when I power this with the'

[07:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'electric only and no solar panels, I\'ve seen this produce when it\'s at 61° working as hard as it can about,80 watts max. That\'s the max I\'ve seen right when it\'s started up and it\'s'

[07:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pushing really hard trying to cool the room. Keep in mind that a 15 amp circuit can do 1,800 watts continuously without tripping the breaker or overheating the wires. Now, obviously, you don\'t want to push it like that all the time, but'

[07:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'let\'s say round up to 1200 watts. That\'s totally fine on a 15 amp circuit. At least in theory, it should not blow the circuit. And we never have in this house with the other 12k BTU air conditioning we had in here that was not on solar.'

[07:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, this one being supplemented with solar, I\'m definitely not ever going to see anywhere near 1,800 watts. So, I am okay putting this on a 15 amp outlet. And I\'m assuming a lot of you probably have 15 amp outlets in your house. So, I'

[07:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'think it is totally fine. Now, I am not a licensed electrician, so take that for what it\'s worth. We\'ve just had no issues doing it that route. Um, my window seal has like a about an inch and a half kind of lip that goes up for the'

