[09:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'took me like 15 minutes. No big deal. Here is a view of the solar panels that I just laid on the ground. What\'s nice about this is you can just go positive to negative, positive to negative, positive to negative all the way across'

[09:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and then just one and then just run one positive and one negative wire. I ran it just all the way up all the way up right through here and it just plugs directly in to the side of'

[09:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the unit. So very simple. And to give you the specs of these solar panels, each of them are 385 watts. Each of them are the open circuit voltage is 48.5 volts. And the amps are 10 amps. So'

[10:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'since I have them connected positive to negative, positive, negative all the way across. I\'m just running one positive and one negative here. I\'ve essentially created one giant solar panel out of these seven at uh 339 volts and 10 amps.'

[10:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So since each panel is 48.5 volts and I have them positive, negative, positive, negative connecting to each other, what happens is the voltage goes up by how'

[10:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'many solar panels you have. So I have 48.5 volts for each panel. I multiply that by 7 and that\'s 339 12 volts. So that\'s the amount of voltage that I\'m'

[10:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'sending back to that air conditioner. And the amps are 10 amps for each of these solar panels. But because I have these in series in positive, negative, positive, negative connection, the amps stay the same. So I\'m running this'

[11:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'string at 339.5 volts at 10 amps, which is well within the limits of the inverter on the window air conditioner. Now, I just set these on the ground temporarily because that\'s'

[11:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the easiest, quickest way to get this thing up and running. If you had this window air conditioner installed in a like a window that\'s on your backyard, you could just throw these on the ground just like this. I\'d probably add some concrete blocks you can get for a couple bucks at Home Depot just to get them up'

[11:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'off the ground. But you could totally run them like this, I think, if you\'re in a low wind area. Like I have no problem doing this for now. But I am going to put some little racks in place and mount these in a better area where'

[11:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it\'s not in the driveway here. But yeah, very simple. Just lay these panels on the ground and get it working. Another thing I wanted to mention is with the package, the signature solar cells that I got here, it comes with 2695 watts worth of solar panels. Um, I think that'

[11:49] [scene:talk]
